/**
 * data/b3/instructions.js — the G1-308 `read-and-do` instruction bank ×11.
 * EN block hand-authored (2026-09-14, the G1-308 build session); the ten
 * non-EN blocks are GENERATED by tools/apply-b3-locale.js from
 * i18n/.draft-b3-<loc>.json after tools/validate-b3-draft.js (never hand-edit a
 * non-EN block here). Contract: docs/worksheet-gen/b3-designs/G1-308-read-and-do.md §4/§5.
 * Read at render ONLY through lib/b3-common.js `bank('instructions', loc)`;
 * every sentence is filled through lib/b3-instructions.js `fillSlots` and the
 * gate (qa/verify-b3-read-and-do.js) re-fills it from THIS file — no
 * `rendered[]` list (two-noun cues are N² per verb).
 *
 * Per-locale block:
 *   nounCase   'keep' | 'lower'   (de keeps the vocab capital; the literals are
 *              stored already cased — the code never re-cases)
 *   mark       'check' | 'cross'  the glyph the `mark` verb asks for
 *   cross      'strike'           the `cross` verb strikes the tile corner to corner
 *   and        the F2 conjunction literal (Phase 2)
 *   endpointForm  which objForms key the `fixed` phrases' {A}/{B} take:
 *              'unique' (en/es/pt/fr/it/nl) | 'dat' (de) | 'gen' (fi) | 'def' (sv/da/no)
 *   verbs      six frames, ids circle · cross · underline · line · mark · write;
 *              ONE object slot each (`line` two; `write` {pl} or fi {part}).
 *              SLOT NAMES ARE FORM SELECTORS (pinned by the build; §4 named the
 *              slots without saying how a cue picks a form): the row's object
 *              under the `unique` cue takes the objForms key the slot names —
 *              {obj}/{all} → unique, {def} → def, {dat} → dat, {gen} → gen,
 *              {a2} → a2, {allDef} → def; under the `all` cue {allDef} → allDef
 *              and every other object slot → all; under `ordinal:k` → ord[k];
 *              under first/last/between/rightof/leftof → the noun-free `fixed`
 *              phrase (its {A}/{B} take endpointForm). The second slot of `line`
 *              names the second noun's form ({obj2} → unique, {dat2} → dat,
 *              {def2} → def, {a2} → a2). A noun whose named form is null is
 *              DROPPED from that (verb, cue), never substituted.
 *   objForms   per vocab key (the theme manifest's vocabKey), WHOLE literals:
 *              unique · all · pl · ord{2..5} · dat · def · defPl · part · gen ·
 *              a2 · reviewed:true (a noun without reviewed:true, or without
 *              unique + all + pl, is not usable; a theme with < 8 usable nouns is
 *              REFUSED for the locale). EN: 133 nouns over the six fan themes
 *              (animals · fruits · vehicles · toys · zoo animals · farm animals);
 *              `baby`, `girl` (a child, not a toy; lookalike of `doll`), `lego`
 *              (a brand; the picture shows three bricks) and `domino` (the
 *              picture shows TWO dominoes — a `write` count would be ambiguous)
 *              are reviewed OUT and absent. Every picture was opened
 *              (_work/G1-308-build.md).
 *   fixed      noun-free position phrases: first · last · ordPic{2..8} ·
 *              between ({A} {B}) · rightof ({A}) · leftof ({A})
 *   truth      F4: { yes, no, frames:[{text, cue, rel?, k?}] } ≥ 8 frames; slots
 *              {n} {pl} {obj} {obj2} only (a frame never OPENS with a noun slot —
 *              the code never capitalises). cue 'count' frames carry rel 'eq' |
 *              'gt' | 'lt' (how {n} relates to the strip count); cue 'ordinal'
 *              frames are WHOLE literals per k (k 2..4, "The third picture is
 *              {obj}."); first/last take {obj}; rightof/leftof take {obj} (unique
 *              on the strip) + {obj2}. {obj}/{obj2} = the noun's `unique` form.
 *   numbers    optional {1..5: word} — F4/F5 print {n} as the word when present,
 *              else the numeral (panel's call per locale)
 *   draw       F5: [{text}] ≥ 4, each with {n} + {pl}
 *   exemplar   the theme rendered when none is pinned
 *   strings    per-face title + instruction (G1-308 = the base; F1..F5 the faces
 *              of §3) — EN is the SOURCE the panels audit.
 *
 * Refusal shape recorded for the panels (design §4 / §7): sv · da · no ship
 * the base ONLY once `def` (+ `defPl`) is authored for every fan-theme noun a
 * def-taking cue uses (unique · all · line · mark · between); until then those
 * blocks carry `def: null` and the base REFUSES (bank() throws while the block
 * is absent; the validator refuses a theme with < 8 def-formed nouns, and a
 * `unique` literal opening with an indefinite article on those locales is a
 * FAIL). de needs a reviewed `dat` for every noun (the 41-key DE_DATIVE_SG
 * table is a cross-check, never the source); fr/it vowel-initial nouns need the
 * elided definite literal or drop from singular cues; fi `write` needs `part`.
 */
